    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Enhance human voice on one audio or video segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --enable TEXT       Enable or disable voice enhancement: true / false (default true)\r\n          --ambient-sound-level TEXT \r\n                              Ambient sound level, 0..100 (default 75)\r\n          --production-path TEXT \r\n                              Existing vocal-enhancement product path\r\n          --from-hd-sounds TEXT \r\n                              Use the HD-sounds path: true / false\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Enable human-voice enhancement\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo voice-enhance --seg-id <AUDIO_OR_VIDEO_UUID>\r\n  # Tune ambient sound level or reuse an existing product\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo voice-enhance --ambient-sound-level 60 \\\r\n      --seg-id <AUDIO_OR_VIDEO_UUID>\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo voice-enhance --production-path /tmp/vocal.wav \\\r\n      --seg-id <AUDIO_OR_VIDEO_UUID>\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - This uses VocalBeautify; it is not sound separation.\r\n  - The target must contain an audio stream.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
